==Russian==
{{wp|ru:}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|ru|насека́ть||to make incisions, to notch}}, a calque of French {{m|fr|insecte}}, from {{m|ru|сечь}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|насеко́мое|pos=a}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-насекомое.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|насеко́мое|+|a=an|hypocor=насеко́мыш}}

# [[insect]]
# {{lb|ru|in the plural}} {{taxfmt|Hexapoda|subphylum}}

====Usage notes====
* The noun '''насеко́мое''' is one of the rare Russian neuter nouns to have animacy. Other neuter nouns with animacy include {{m|ru|живо́тное}}, {{m|ru|существо́}},  чадо, чудовище, дитя, etc.

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table|насеко́мое|+|a=an}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ru|бука́шка}}
* {{l|ru|козя́вка}}

====Derived terms====
